# Slow Journey Cursor Rule

This repository is a Flutter daily-rhythm app (offline-first, Phase 1, no network).
Follow Duka Mkononi–style quality gates adapted for this product.

## Scope and stack
- App root: `lib/`, `test/`, `android/`, `ios/`
- Stack: Flutter, Provider, Drift + SQLite, local notifications
- Display name: **Slow Journey**. Package id: `chingalo.family.slowjourney`
- Always follow `.cursor/skills/slow-journey-project/SKILL.md`
- Offline schema / counters / `syncStatus`: `.cursor/skills/slow-journey-offline/SKILL.md`
- User-facing labels: `.cursor/skills/slow-journey-localization/SKILL.md` (`lib/l10n/app_en.arb`; English first)
- Contributor / OSS files: `.cursor/skills/slow-journey-community-docs/SKILL.md`

## Required workflow before finishing
1. Run `git status` and `git diff`
2. `flutter analyze` must print **No issues found!**
3. `flutter test` must pass
4. After Drift changes: `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs`
5. After label/copy changes: update `lib/l10n/app_en.arb` and run `flutter gen-l10n`
6. If architecture, modules, reminders, schema, or setup behavior changed, update the matching docs under `docs/`
7. If end-user-visible behavior changed, update the matching guide under `docs/user-guides/`
8. If setup, stack, modules, env, quality gates, security surfaces, or contributor workflow changed, update community-health files (see `slow-journey-community-docs`)
9. Do not add network, DHIS2, or Community features in Phase 1
10. Update `.cursor/` if conventions drift

## Architecture
- Logic in `lib/core/services/*`, not widgets
- Shared UI in `lib/core/components/*`
- Package imports: `package:slowjourney/...`
- Persist locally with `syncStatus`
- Never commit secrets

## Naming
- Meaningful names; no `i` / `j` / `k` loop indexes
- No inline `//` comments in Dart
- Tests describe behavior

## Data safety
- Append migrations; derived schema version
- Do not rename persisted columns casually

## Documentation sync
When behavior changes, update the relevant docs in the same change set:
- `README.md` and `docs/README.md`
- `docs/architecture/` (overview, offline-storage, data-sync)
- `docs/diagrams/` (startup, navigation, module wiring)
- `docs/features/*.md` (module/capability/brand)
- `docs/development/*.md` (setup, env, testing, naming, localization)
- `docs/user-guides/*.md` (friendly guides when UX/flows change)
- `docs/plans/` only for work that is **not shipped yet**
- `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `docs/GETTING_STARTED.md`
- `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` and `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`

Skip docs only for pure typo/format-only edits with no behavior change.
